+## Living tableaux — OD-2026-11-04-A
+
+Dedicated `PRODUCTION-CONTRACTS-LIVING-TABLEAUX-1` / [OD-2026-11-04-A](../autonomy/LIVING_TABLEAUX_OPERATOR_DECISION_2026-11-04.md), set 1.13.0. For code-animated sequences on existing approved tableaux only, it narrows two rules of the cinematic retirement section: "Stop new cinematic … production, including pilot generalization" and "No video delay or empty replacement interlude". Every other rule of OD-2026-10-24-A stays in force: zero active video; no video playback, preload, video-derived hold or shipped MP4; no generated or new illustrated image; no illustrated montage; no video or keyframe generation; no MiniMax; the eight historical identities and every archive.
+
+- **Medium.** A living tableau is a short sequence animated by code on an existing approved painted tableau. It may use light, fire, smoke, weather, a slow camera, and pixel figures drawn at the tableau's grain from existing Character V2 sheets or portraits. It uses no WebGL, video element, recorded media, generated image or new illustration.
+- **Moments, exhaustively.** `bois_clair_arrival`, before `village_choice`. `bois_clair_saved`, after a `village_defense` victory with `missionSuccess` and without `missionGreed`, before `village_defense_aftermath`. `bois_clair_sacrificed`, after a `village_raid` victory with `missionGreed`, before `village_raid_aftermath`. `lion_judgement`, before `lion_finale_judgement`. These beat ids name the moment only: no video slot is reopened and no video descriptor is activated. A sequence opens no new beat, and replaces no dialogue, choice, tableau or combat. The opening sequence stays governed by OD-2026-11-02-A, with its own length and approved captions; it may share the player's code only.
+- **When it plays.** A sequence plays only when its beat opens live for the first time. A revisit of a beat that RunSystem has resolved, a reload or a resume goes straight to the dialogue, in line with the POI navigation rule that resolved revisits replay no one-shot presentation. This needs no new save field, and nothing transient is serialized.
+- **Length and agency.** At most 30 seconds, or 40 for `lion_judgement`. Click, Enter, or a visible skip control that meets the keyboard and focus rules of UI_AND_ACCESSIBILITY, moves to the next shot or straight to the dialogue. A sequence never blocks input, and never delays a save, reward, choice, combat or defeat recovery. A missing image or a script failure goes straight to the dialogue, which opens on the same first step as without the sequence.
+- **Canon.** No new text: these sequences have no captions. A sequence shows only facts already established at its point of the route, as listed in the moment table that OD-2026-11-04-A approves, and never what the following dialogue says first. It never plays a choice, outcome, verdict or consequence before its canonical owner resolves it. A branch sequence reads the resolved outcome only through the existing presentation trigger. The `lion_judgement` sequence shows Alaric alone, without the champion, and ends before Alaric speaks; the Alaric climax is unchanged.
+- **Cast.** At most four visible narrative actors. Extras are moving scenery: they have no dialogue, focus or facing relation, are drawn behind the narrative actors, number at most twelve, and are never counted as actors or fed to the relational staging planner. Character V2 identities, equipment and authored facing hold.
+- **Animated backdrop.** During the following dialogue, its tableau may keep animated light, fire, smoke and distant extras under the same cast rule. That changes no staging, focus or text.
+- **Reduced motion.** OS or game reduced motion keeps a fixed camera and turns travel into fades. Fire, light and wind may stay animated. Every shot keeps its information.
+- **Audio.** A sequence takes the mood of its following dialogue through the existing mood table, with no new table key tied to the sequence. It adds no track or cue. Cinematic audio and voices stay DEFERRED.
+- **Ownership.** One shared presentation-only player serves these moments. It creates no route, outcome, resource or save field.
+- **Order.** A mockup of `bois_clair_arrival`, judged in motion by the operator, precedes the three other sequences and the animated backdrop. Operator artistic acceptance is by viewing.
